+STATUS: IN-PROGRESS — local implementation, not released or independently graded.
+
+# CXN3-FIX: bounded v2 request input
+
+The unsigned oversized-request probe expects400 or413. The former shared handler returned401 because authentication ran before the size check. A new regression suite reproduced that discrepancy for missing, small and oversized Content-Length values, UTF-8 byte sizes and chunked input. It also exposed pending reads/cancellation with no bounded completion. Initial working-tree result:8failed and16passed; raw evidence is preserved on the ledger in reports/cards/CXN3-FIX/local-checks/body-limit-before.log.
+
+The shared handler now bounds actual input bytes before authentication. It preserves the8192-byte limit and uses a single10-second body-read deadline. Aborts and oversized input cancel the producer without waiting indefinitely for cancellation. JSON/UTF-8 validation still follows authentication and budget admission; ordinary unsigned malformed/empty bodies remain401. Valid authenticated requests retain their identity, object payload and budget behavior. OPTIONS, method refusal, CORS and Retry-After behavior remain covered.
+
+Local working-tree checks:27new regressions passed; Supabase typecheck passed after an explicit HeadersInit annotation fixed a test typing error; the complete Supabase suite passed575tests in33files. The earlier typecheck error remains in typecheck-r1.log. No existing assertion, skip, retry or test timeout was changed. These working-tree results are not yet exact-commit full-gate certification.
+
+Scope: Tier1 is supabase/functions/_shared/v2/http.ts and supabase/tests/src/v2-body-limits.test.ts. Tier2 adds apps/web/e2e/server/request-body-limits.spec.ts to exercise all nine routes through the existing loopback HTTP/PGlite server, plus this report and the linked decision/index. The wire checks retain the existing15-second diagnostic timeout and disable retries. No authentication-token verifier, SIWE code, database schema, player state, gameplay rules, contracts, dependencies, environment values or frontend flags changed. The intended behavior is a repair to an existing input limit, not a new gameplay feature.
+
+The body-read policy and tradeoff are documented in docs/decisions/cxn3-request-body-limits.md. The timeout is an input-resource limit, not proof that historical live timeouts have been fixed. The existing15-second live checker timeout remains unchanged. The first wire probe over-constrained the mission's400-or413contract to400 and failed9cases because the unchanged local transport rejects at8192bytes with413. Its source/log are retained; the corrected wire test still rejects401 and does not certify the handler branch hidden behind that transport guard. Direct handler regressions and later live checks remain required. Current live findings, partial export limitations and the repair's position before CXN3 remain on the ledger.
+
+Pending: exact-commit verification, deliberate mutants, full root/build/browser/UI/public-config/wrapper gates, applicable independent review, actual-main integration, PR publication, release/rollback proof and fresh live validation. The user forbids subagents/helpers; coordinator self-review must not be described as independent grading. No source push, merge or backend deployment has occurred for this item.
